    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d559">

                <pb facs="0563" n="529" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg529"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Woodford to Mr.
                            Sherman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Sebastian, Spain</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1897-09-21"><hi rendition="#italic">September
                                21, 1897</hi></date>. (Received Oct. 4.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 30.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your No. 23, of August 28, 1897, inclosing for my information the
                    correspondence had by your Department touching the request of the military
                    governor of Santiago for list of American property. I note the Department’s
                    reply through the consul-general at Havana, and shall maintain with earnestness
                    the position therein taken.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stewart L.
                    Woodford.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
